{
  "$comment": "HAND-EDITED test vectors of the settings schema export: per row, values a validator must accept and values it must refuse (accepts and refuses in schemas/settings/settings-schema.json), so another validator (the daemon's config actor) can prove it agrees with the app's. A row takes the set of its validation domain (domains: the row's validation in row-facts.json) when there is one, else the set of its kind (kinds: the export's kind, and choice_list for a string_list row with choices). {\"$sample\": NAME} stands for values taken from the row: choices (each choice value, in order), choices_reversed, first_choice (\"a\" when none), min, max, mid, below (min minus the span), above (max plus the span; the span is max minus min, at least 1) and url_key; an object member named $url_key takes the row's url_key as its name. scripts/cmux-next/gen-settings-sources.py writes the Swift copy (SettingsSchema+Samples.generated.swift).",
  "kinds": {
    "toggle": {
      "accept": [
        true,
        false
      ],
      "refuse": [
        "true",
        1,
        null
      ]
    },
    "choice": {
      "accept": [
        {"$sample": "choices"}
      ],
      "refuse": [
        "__not_a_choice__",
        1,
        true
      ]
    },
    "choice_or_number": {
      "accept": [
        {"$sample": "choices"},
        {"$sample": "min"},
        {"$sample": "max"},
        {"$sample": "mid"}
      ],
      "refuse": [
